                  <provenance>The name(s) of the original donor(s) has been erased from <ref target="#a1">Additio 1</ref> and <ref target="#a2">Additio 2</ref>. 
                     The note in the Latin script, ‘Liturgy’, and number ‘484’ written on <locus target="#1r"/> indicate that the book was likely taken as booty from the church <placeName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/INS0101MadhaneAlam">Madḫāne ʿĀlam</placeName>
                     (founded by <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS9430Tewodros">Tewodros II</persName>, r. <date>1855–68</date>). The name of the monastery of <placeName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/INS0105DD">ʾAbuna ʾAragāwi</placeName>, located in the upper margin of <locus target="#2r"/>, 
                     is most likely written over an erased name of the church <placeName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/INS0101MadhaneAlam">Madḫāne ʿĀlam</placeName>.</provenance></history>
